00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:25.280
12th Communication Company and 12th Engineering Company,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.530
on the eastern side, deploy to Area 45.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:31.370
Pilots of the 2nd and 3rd Mobile Suit
Corps, assemble in Briefing Room 38.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.540
13th Supply Regiment, deploy when finished loading the goods.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.960
This is the 42nd Communication Corps,
preparations are complete.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.170
We will depart immediately.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.460
Roger.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.090
The 37th team will take care of the
transportation of the medical team.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.880
17th Tank Force, deploying now.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.190
The weather in the eastern coastal region is deteriorating.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:58.520
Incoming transmission from Naval Headquarters.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.980
Code 051, transferring it to A02.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.950
It is believed that Sri Lanka has been hit by a large tsunami

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.110
No information has come in yet.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.000
All of Salvador's regions are flooded.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:13.410
I don't think Dullindal had a hand in this.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.010
Dogachhia is requesting for deployment.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.000
The Atlantic Federation hasn't taken

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.250
a firm stance on this incident yet either.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.760
Viewing the Santos area, Route 21 is flooded.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.170
There are no alternative routes available.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:27.030
I am left speechless in front of this unbelievable devastation.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.400
I believe the pain we experienced is deep,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.740
and the sorrow is endless.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.060
Route 7 isn't usable since it's flooded.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.480
However, our friends on Earth,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.430
Enter the city using Junction 65.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:39.110
please stand strong after this day of despair.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.900
Please stay where you are if you're
not in a life threatening state.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.300
Anybody else with injuries, please signal
us with smoke candles or other means.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:04:59.720
All right, get him out of here.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.860
Since we can't call for someone to pick
us up, we'll just have to use our privileges.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.140
Take all the wounded to the B20 shelter.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:13.800
Major!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.640
Oh, it's Combat Commander Reyes.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.530
The emergency medical team will arrive in an hour!

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.140
I'm a sergeant now.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.220
I'm a civilian now.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:24.030
After I'm done with this mission,
will you take me out for a drink again?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.990
Sure. I'll keep that in mind.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.330
Do you know him?

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.040
He used to be my commanding officer.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.570
Note: DSSD stands for Deep Space Survey and Development Organization.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.580
I heard that he retired to a private
organization called the DSSD.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.840
He's the legendary Demon Director.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:37.460
Then, he's that Major Edmond Ducreau?

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.620
Please send the supplies to us immediately.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.220
We're currently short on food supplies,
drinking water, and medical supplies.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.550
Mama!

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.790
I'll help you find your mama, okay?

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.770
He wants us to lend him a helicopter?!

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.230
Yes, sir...

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.400
The people right over there.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:53.370
Hey you! You understand the situation, don't you?

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.610
We don't even have a single wash basin that's free right now!

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.780
Don't you understand that?!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:58.900
Please wait a second.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.280
Are you all right?

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.780
Edmond Ducreau.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.860
DSSD Technology Development
Center Vice Director of Security.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.360
This here's Selene McGriff.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.620
DSSD Employee.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.710
I suppose it can't be helped.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:16.840
But Colonel...

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.220
Although, it's not like we have one to give you.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.550
What was that explosion?

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:23.550
We're currently gathering information on it.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:25.930
It fired at us!

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:35.360
What is that?

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.000
Hey..!

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.670
Is this war?

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:55.700
What has Military Headquarters said on this matter?

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:56.380
Yes.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.340
Yes, I understand.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.160
No, we haven't received it yet.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.290
Let's hurry.

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.080
401 is waiting for you.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:05.370
Drainage operation of Exhaust Port 4 is 80 percent complete.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.630
How's the flooding of Block N4?

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:08.790
It's already at its limit!

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.450
It may collapse at any minute now!

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:13.380
1 hour and 23 minutes until shuttle launch.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.950
All sectors, report the launching procedure
up to now and after its completion as well.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.700
Still haven't gotten a hold of Selene?

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:21.450
Not yet.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:25.180
In the worst case scenario, we may have
to consider launching it without her.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.510
All available tanks, head out!

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:39.490
4th Tank Force, heading nut!

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:40.880
I'm sorry.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:41.420
Headquarters!

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.760
This is the maximum capacity of this boat.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.300
This is the 31st Platoon.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.180
31st Platoon, what's the matter?

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.180
I understand that.

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.680
Give cover to the 4th Platoon.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.110
In the operation area?

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:49.380
Are there any–

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:54.230
Headquarters?!

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.390
Headquarters, what's the matter?!

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.100
Headquarters, please respond!

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:57.770
Headquarters!

00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:58.610
Was Headquarters taken out?

00:07:58.610 --> 00:07:59.310
We're not sure yet.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.610
Are you serious?

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:01.220
Yeah, of course.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.980
I plan on heading back to the Center as soon as possible.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:07.630
I pray on behalf of your launch's success.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:14.850
Tell Sol to buy me a good gift from space.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.540
Something that's useful in seducing women.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:22.460
Did you know, while on duty you need
to request these things in advance?

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.340
You may be right about that.

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.690
Take the path to the bridge at the northern part of the city.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.860
Don't go anywhere close to the center of the city.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:29.890
Yes, sir.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.650
Get a hold of yourself.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.890
Are you okay?

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.370
Major!

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:56.570
My bad, for having you end up turning in a written report.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:57.900
Not at all.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.100
I'm honored to be able to ride with you again. Major.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:03.240
As long as the command post isn't functional,

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:06.580
I have to make the decisions for the
most effective outcome on my own.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.500
You've grown a lot, haven't you?

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:13.340
I will observe your commanding
once again for future reference.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.160
Huh, Selene?

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.080
Did you have another fight with the Director?

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.670
You think that you're always right.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.920
Well, you are always right.

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.800
So, what's wrong?

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:49.500
Hold on.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:53.160
First you came to complain, and
now you're going to lecture me?

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:54.760
Give me a break.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.220
I'm aware of it.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:02.840
Even a Coordinator takes two years to pass
the first class controller qualification exam.

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:08.440
In that case, a Natural like me will have
to spend six years to pass it, right?

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:11.940
Hey... Why did you decide to join the DSSD?

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:15.910
Besides as an excuse to see me.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:17.400
Oh yeah.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:21.260
You can't use seeing Dr. Maria Ittou
of Laboratory 1 as an excuse either.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:23.750
What about you?

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:26.120
I'm the one asking the question right now.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.910
It's not like I have a real answer for it.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:35.250
I just wanted to look up for the time being.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.500
Up?

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:42.880
Like when you look to your side, you get jealous
of them and want it for yourself, don't you?

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.800
And if you look down, there's somebody
you can help with your current stature.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:50.600
It's fine if they seek your help,

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:54.690
but what if there's nobody weaker than you?

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:58.730
At that moment you ask yourself, "What am I going to do?"

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.820
That's why I wanted to secure a position where I could look up.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.300
Block N4 has collapsed.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:19.340
Skip pages 243-324 of the shuttle launch process.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.710
You should go get ready now.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:23.510
Yes.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:27.180
Dr. McGriff has arrived at Gate 23.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.190
The shuttle launch will be held in 15 minutes.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:34.080
Stop the supply of electricity to all
blocks besides Block 3, 4, and 7.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.560
We will secure the electricity in preparation for an emergency.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.220
This is Chief of Sector 24, Victor Rodriguez, no anomalies found.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:40.950
Ready anytime.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.000
This is Chief of Sector 4, George Gida, all clear.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.370
Sectors 13 and 14 have flooded.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:48.450
Block off passages B44, B45, F11, F12, and F13!

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:59.630
Close in as much as possible while
he's distracted by the other tanks!

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:00.460
Yes, sir.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.520
Sergeant, set the rapid-fire interval to .5 seconds.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.850
That's absurd!

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:06.730
The barrels won't hold!

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.140
I don't mind.

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.730
We're only using it once, anyhow.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:11.850
Where's Ed?

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:15.790
He wanted you to get him a gift to seduce women.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.540
Then, what do you want?

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:19.320
Huh?

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:24.910
From what I know, there's no other woman
besides you who he'd want to seduce.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.320
Not to mention, women pretend they
don't know even if they're aware of it.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.260
Close in as much as possible!

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.310
Or else we won't be able to pierce through that armor!

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:46.060
Roger!

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.190
Fire!

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.400
T-30 seconds until launch.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:12.160
Diagnostic computer, initiating controls.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.300
Block A25, flooded.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:18.050
A32, Telegram Room, flooded.

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:20.230
BI4, Cable Tunnel, flooded.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.960
Continuing launch countdown.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:23.130
15.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:24.210
14.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:24.880
13.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:25.800
12.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:28.270
Sector 3 flooded by 40 percent.

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:26.960
11.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:28.270
10.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:28.880
9.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:30.850
Ignition of main engine.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:32.590
5.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:33.470
4.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:34.470
3.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.230
Shuttle lifting off.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:43.950
Shuttle has lift off.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.420
The enemy's movement has stopped!

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.250
Do not give up now!

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.860
Fire all the missiles you have at it!

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:00.750
DH-74, give it some incendiary bombs from the skies!

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.040
Bake it good!

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.170
C-Children...?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:43.380
Why are these children in here?

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.550
It seems the revolt by the ZAFT mobile suits

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:48.340
It seems the ZAFT remnants who believed in Patrick Zala

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:47.430
in the northern part of South America has finally ended

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:50.310
The forces in the southern part of Australia

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.300
are revolting at various places.

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:51.310
are still resisting strenuously.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:54.880
It seems that PLANT is denying having
taken any part in this incident.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.170
An emergency rescue signal from the Kirgiz plant.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:14:59.610
It's ZAFT mobile suits.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:03.240
That place is developing a new driving force computer..!

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.630
Send them in.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:05.130
Yes. sir.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:11.990
GAT-X1022 Blu Duel, activation of all systems confirmed.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:18.350
GAT-X103AP Verde Buster, activation of all systems confirmed.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:24.380
Continuing with GAT-X105E Strike Noir,

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:26.180
activation of all systems confirmed.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:37.450
Sven Cal Vayan, Strike Noir, heading out!

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.410
Reinforcements are here!

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:12.850
Jeez. Don't go taking all the kills.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:33.870
Yes.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.290
The insurrection forces at Kirqiz have been eliminated.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:42.620
However, though they were a guerilla unit,
they were better armed than we had anticipated.

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:45.710
It seems they went into combat
expecting to face the Destroy units.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.090
Yes. We're in a critical situation right now.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:55.600
I think it would be wise to refrain from a large-scale retaliation.

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:57.730
In that case...

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.640
My father's name is Alphonso Rossi.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.340
My mother's name is Ecatrina Rossi.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:06.890
They were both doctors.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.920
However, Naturals killed my parents.

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:11.980
Just because they were Coordinators.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.820
Naturals are a bunch of savages.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.080
We are going to get our revenge right now.

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:19.400
However, Naturals are the ones at fault.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.360
Kill all Naturals!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.250
Death to Blue Cosmos!

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:29.880
The video you have just witnessed was sent to the local
TV station after the terrorist incident at Fortaleza.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:38.510
It is believed that this incident was backed by
Coordinator activists supporting terrorist attacks.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:47.490
Ever since the fall of Junius Seven, scattered terrorist
attacks have been emerging worldwide.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:52.850
The authorities strongly criticize that the Coordinator's
inhumane actions were evident in the terrorist attacks.

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:58.430
It has been announced that the countries concerned
are to develop strict countermeasures immediately.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.670
"Inhumane," they say.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:07.880
My teacher once said, "The only good
Coordinator is a dead Coordinator."

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:25.110
I see. You want to become an astronomer, huh?

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:29.320
Well then, I'll have to buy you a telescope
for your next birthday present.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.320
What?! Really?!

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.780
Isn't that nice?

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:33.610
Yes.

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:36.580
It's almost time for the Lyrid Meteor Shower!

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.090
Thank you, Papa!

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:02.080
Our target is the Coordinators' refugee camp.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:06.780
It has been confirmed that this camp is
actually a disguised terrorist training facility.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:11.900
Your mission is to destroy this
facility and eliminate all terrorists.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:16.740
Our enemy, will it be restricted to just the terrorists, sir?

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:21.930
Can you tell apart the terrorists from the refugees?

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.140
No, sir.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.890
Well, that's how it is.

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:09.900
Coordinators are the ones who killed our parents.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.980
Coordinators are the devils of space.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:17.110
All Coordinators must be killed in the interest of peace.

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:20.880
For justice, and for a pure, blue world.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:23.490
We must kill all Coordinators.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:24.290
Fire.

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:38.980
Pick up the pace!

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:41.030
Last year's team was a lot faster!

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:42.300
Thirty seconds more!

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:43.100
Hurry it up!

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:54.070
You should've informed everyone that you
only had seven magazines, am I correct?

00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:55.480
Yes, sir!

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:57.530
Should I have been responsible for checking it?

00:21:57.530 --> 00:21:58.110
No, sir!

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.060
You were ordered out to the front with
two others on a reconnaissance mission,

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:05.690
but you only had one spare magazine with you.

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:07.820
"Oh, I know. I'll just keep it to myself."

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:09.900
That's what you were thinking at the time.

00:22:10.150 --> 00:22:11.070
Was that okay?

00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:14.160
Three laps around Runway B.

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:14.990
Yes, sir!

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:10.280
DSSD Troya Station

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:10.280
DSSD Troya Station

00:23:11.010 --> 00:23:12.050
Are you ready?

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:14.550
Yes. I'll be out in a second.

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:16.760
Sorry for keeping you waiting.

00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:18.380
Were you able to sleep well?

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:19.060
Yes.

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:21.490
You put your hair up, haven't you?

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:22.570
Yes.

00:23:22.570 --> 00:23:23.820
Well then, let's get going.

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.400
The response time is still too slow.

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:32.200
Yes.

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:33.910
Dr. Segawa.

00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:35.950
Oh, it's Selene.

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:38.980
How's your research of energy in a vacuum coming along?

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:41.390
Oh. That's been canceled.

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:44.420
I've been working on this huge hand for a while now.

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:46.690
Are you going to be testing that already?

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:47.900
Not yet.

00:23:48.010 --> 00:23:50.710
I'm going to have Dr. Moriseiwa check out the actual product.

00:23:51.520 --> 00:23:55.440
Kram Company is on trial again for the patent rights.

00:23:55.440 --> 00:23:56.900
How troublesome.

00:23:57.520 --> 00:24:00.820
What? New York's stocks fell again.

00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:02.990
It's because they're having a war.

00:24:03.530 --> 00:24:05.110
Dr. Nostravich.

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:05.640
Huh?

00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:07.780
Oh. it's Selene

00:24:07.780 --> 00:24:09.580
Are you doing your actual job once in a while?

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:15.990
Analyzing stock fluctuations is about
the only job a mathematician has.

00:24:20.090 --> 00:24:22.340
When will the B Ring be completed?

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:24.380
About a year or so.

00:24:27.760 --> 00:24:31.700
Wow. So this is 401's AI unit?

00:24:32.520 --> 00:24:37.040
Although it can only recognize the information
that's been inputted and process it,

00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:41.190
as it builds up its experience, it'll be
able to make its own judgment.

00:24:41.190 --> 00:24:45.820
When that happens, someday, it'll be able to probe planets.

00:24:47.740 --> 00:24:49.820
This is the optional cockpit.

00:24:49.820 --> 00:24:52.030
I heard it was a two-seater.

00:24:52.040 --> 00:24:57.830
At first, a person will pilot it while the
AI learns from the pilot's behavior.

00:24:58.100 --> 00:25:03.130
So when a person pilots it, this thing
goes in where that AI unit is at?

00:25:03.340 --> 00:25:03.960
Yes.

00:25:04.760 --> 00:25:08.130
By the way, what's the status on the
Voiture unit I asked you to build?

00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:09.570
It's already been completed.

00:25:10.220 --> 00:25:11.350
Solar sail.

00:25:12.100 --> 00:25:16.310
The possibility of flying faster through
space without the use of hydraulics.

00:25:16.940 --> 00:25:19.600
You have given me the opportunity
to take on an interesting project.

00:25:20.440 --> 00:25:25.900
During experimentation, we'll set the output of
Apollon A to one percent, and imitate the solar winds.

00:25:26.350 --> 00:25:29.890
We probably won't be able to obtain a
recognizable speed if we don't do that at least.

00:25:51.640 --> 00:25:55.040
Jeez, these guys are so persistent, I'm getting tired of it.

00:25:55.100 --> 00:25:58.240
Maybe they all want to have a fun time with you.

00:26:14.530 --> 00:26:15.080
Mudie!

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:18.200
This isn't looking too good...

00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:21.500
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:27:05.530 --> 00:27:07.030
What the hell happened here?!

00:27:07.090 --> 00:27:08.630
Stop screwing around!

00:27:08.630 --> 00:27:09.760
Hey, Mudie!

00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:11.010
You've got to be kidding me...!

00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:12.660
Mudie!

00:27:31.810 --> 00:27:32.810
Whoops.

00:27:33.320 --> 00:27:34.590
What's with her?

00:27:34.600 --> 00:27:37.400
It's probably a ruined Extended.

00:27:37.700 --> 00:27:38.410
What?

00:27:38.910 --> 00:27:40.200
They don't live too long.

00:27:42.330 --> 00:27:43.910
We've received new orders.

00:27:43.920 --> 00:27:45.290
This time we were ordered out to space.

00:27:45.290 --> 00:27:45.960
Space?

00:27:46.500 --> 00:27:50.960
We were ordered to steal the DSSD's mobile
suit that they're building at the space station.

00:27:51.590 --> 00:27:54.680
We have received permission to kill any personnel.

00:27:55.260 --> 00:27:55.880
I see.

00:28:00.180 --> 00:28:02.180
You're always like that.

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:05.390
Making that "It has nothing to do with me" expression.

00:28:08.820 --> 00:28:11.620
We're allowed to kill them, you know...

00:28:20.290 --> 00:28:21.570
Energy cable detached.

00:28:24.010 --> 00:28:27.060
Laser Transmission Station
Apollon A

00:28:24.010 --> 00:28:27.060
Laser Transmission Station
Apollon A

00:28:24.490 --> 00:28:28.020
Laser Transmission Station Apollon A to Troya Control.

00:28:28.790 --> 00:28:31.530
We will now transfer control to 401.

00:28:35.590 --> 00:28:36.360
Completed.

00:28:36.610 --> 00:28:38.570
401, you may now start up.

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:06.210
We will now begin testing the Voiture Lumire.

00:29:06.340 --> 00:29:06.980
Roger.

00:29:07.670 --> 00:29:11.130
401, please move to the experiment point.

00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:21.700
Hey, don't you think it's a bit rude to the AI if we call it 401?

00:29:22.310 --> 00:29:23.060
Huh?

00:29:24.680 --> 00:29:26.430
Edmond said this before, right?

00:29:26.430 --> 00:29:28.390
"Look up and move on.

00:29:28.390 --> 00:29:33.220
Because you'll become jealous or frightened
if you look to your sides or below you.

00:29:34.530 --> 00:29:35.770
The one who looks up.

00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:38.940
The one who'll look at the stars beyond.

00:29:39.990 --> 00:29:41.110
Stargazer."

00:29:46.200 --> 00:29:47.450
That's right.

00:29:56.590 --> 00:29:58.140
Activate Voiture Lumire.

00:30:12.730 --> 00:30:14.310
Voiture Lumire.

00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:19.690
The takeoff observation values of the quantum mirror
surfaces are within the expected range in all fields.

00:30:20.410 --> 00:30:22.160
Emit the propulsion beam.

00:30:22.200 --> 00:30:24.080
Emitting the propulsion beam.

00:30:42.470 --> 00:30:44.390
The propulsion beam has made contact.

00:30:44.970 --> 00:30:46.260
No system abnormalities found.

00:30:48.060 --> 00:30:50.310
This is the station's observation room.

00:30:50.310 --> 00:30:53.980
We have confirmed 401's Voiture Lumire's acceleration cruise.

00:30:54.760 --> 00:30:56.220
Congratulations 401.

00:30:56.390 --> 00:30:58.640
No, Stargazer.

00:31:00.640 --> 00:31:01.480
Thank you.

00:31:12.890 --> 00:31:17.950
93rd Communications Satellite

00:31:12.890 --> 00:31:17.950
93rd Communications Satellite

00:31:22.060 --> 00:31:23.850
Security lack disarmament successful.

00:31:23.940 --> 00:31:25.520
We're moving on to the next phase.

00:31:25.640 --> 00:31:28.180
24 minutes until the mission completion deadline.

00:31:28.180 --> 00:31:28.680
Roger.

00:31:29.730 --> 00:31:34.950
For a couple of months, ever since the Junius Seven
Incident, while PLANT and the EAF were fighting it out,

00:31:35.110 --> 00:31:40.490
the battlefield has relocated to space,
fallowing the departure of Djibril from Earth.

00:31:41.490 --> 00:31:44.660
How has his progress been ever since?

00:31:44.660 --> 00:31:48.650
It's still not enough. He still can only
process the information we send him.

00:31:48.730 --> 00:31:52.860
And for him to be able to make choices on
his own will take at least 10,000 hours.

00:31:56.570 --> 00:31:58.850
There's an unnerving rumor going around.

00:31:59.830 --> 00:32:03.900
A division of the EAF has shown interest
in the AI component of the Stargazer.

00:32:04.680 --> 00:32:07.810
They're being pushed in a tight corner as it is.

00:32:13.170 --> 00:32:18.510
But the "New Social Status System" that
Dullindal talks about... What could this be–

00:32:21.080 --> 00:32:24.080
DSSD Station Control Room

00:32:21.080 --> 00:32:24.080
DSSD Station Control Room

00:32:21.530 --> 00:32:23.570
The Interplanetary Communication System is offline.

00:32:23.570 --> 00:32:25.320
We're not receiving any telemetry on any of the channels.

00:32:25.320 --> 00:32:28.120
Data link is severed. The back-up won't work either!

00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:29.930
Mobile suit unit approaching!

00:32:30.630 --> 00:32:35.880
This is the Nana Buluku of the EAF's
81st Independent Mobile Battalion.

00:32:36.470 --> 00:32:39.300
We will take hold of your station now.

00:32:39.740 --> 00:32:43.950
We have orders that allow us to use force without prejudice.

00:32:44.090 --> 00:32:48.760
The 81st Independent Mobile Battalion is... Phantom Pain!

00:32:48.760 --> 00:32:54.020
It's true that this station was first created by ZAFT, but
now we're an independent and completely neutral base!

00:32:54.170 --> 00:32:56.880
We're even helping out the EAF with technical problems!

00:32:57.760 --> 00:33:00.090
Maintenance crews, hurry up repairing communication lines!

00:33:00.770 --> 00:33:04.820
Contact EAF Headquarters, and tell
them to stop this operation at once!

00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:09.520
It's probably futile. From the start,
they have been aiming for this station.

00:33:12.250 --> 00:33:14.880
Send out the soldiers. We're taking over the interior.

00:33:25.380 --> 00:33:28.630
I'll never forgive you...! I'll never forgive any of you!

00:33:29.650 --> 00:33:30.600
Close the port!

00:33:35.300 --> 00:33:37.550
This is the 42nd Launch Bay Operations' control room.

00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:43.400
This is the 16th unit. The 42nd Launch Bay has been secured.

00:33:49.450 --> 00:33:51.740
Enemy soldiers have arrived at block B2.

00:33:51.740 --> 00:33:53.980
Send people over to that block immediately!

00:33:54.060 --> 00:33:57.900
Chief, evacuate all civilians to the B Ring.

00:33:57.910 --> 00:33:59.040
Understood.

00:33:59.040 --> 00:34:00.620
What about my research material–

00:33:59.990 --> 00:34:02.110
Where are Selene and Sol?

00:34:12.510 --> 00:34:13.970
Odalel unit! Ges unit! Contact lost!

00:34:14.060 --> 00:34:16.310
Sections D and F, communication severed.

00:34:16.310 --> 00:34:18.560
The 3rd Barricade has been breached!

00:34:19.170 --> 00:34:20.090
Scared?

00:34:21.050 --> 00:34:24.010
Enemy soldiers have also arrived at the 32nd Launch Bay!

00:34:24.770 --> 00:34:25.980
You're right...

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:29.650
I'm sorry. Having to make you kill people...

00:34:30.530 --> 00:34:31.240
Even this child...

00:34:42.050 --> 00:34:44.090
Astray Unit 1, signal lost.

00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:46.870
Krom unit and Kam unit damaged! They can no longer fight!

00:34:47.280 --> 00:34:49.330
There's no use... Those two are too strong!

00:34:50.680 --> 00:34:52.730
It's impossible... The enemies are veteran fighters!

00:34:52.890 --> 00:34:56.600
Signal, all green. Human control input, enabled.

00:34:57.150 --> 00:34:58.280
Protection, close.

00:34:58.350 --> 00:34:58.970
Signal, lost.

00:34:58.980 --> 00:35:00.270
Protection, closed.

00:35:07.430 --> 00:35:08.970
The 4th Barricade has been overrun!

00:35:09.810 --> 00:35:13.140
Have we still not been able to contact EAF Headquarters?

00:35:13.390 --> 00:35:15.270
We're doing our best on the repairs!

00:35:18.150 --> 00:35:21.070
Let's end this. We can't let any more lives be lost.

00:35:21.320 --> 00:35:24.070
This is the Stargazer. We will now launch.

00:35:24.610 --> 00:35:25.860
Stargazer?

00:35:27.870 --> 00:35:32.290
The N-jammer canceller is still working.
We can only use the power cells.

00:35:32.430 --> 00:35:33.590
What's our autonomy?

00:35:33.590 --> 00:35:35.430
At full power. 17 minutes.

00:35:35.430 --> 00:35:36.510
Use it sparingly.

00:35:44.090 --> 00:35:45.720
Take them down with one shot!

00:35:45.840 --> 00:35:46.720
Don't lose concentration!

00:35:46.780 --> 00:35:47.200
Roger.

00:35:55.190 --> 00:35:57.020
Only 5 enemy mobile suits left.

00:35:57.310 --> 00:35:59.310
Heading, 3 o'clock. That one looks tough.

00:36:01.570 --> 00:36:02.110
That guy, huh.

00:36:14.790 --> 00:36:16.040
All right, contact the ship.

00:36:17.420 --> 00:36:19.210
2nd Platoon, target captured.

00:36:19.460 --> 00:36:22.000
"We will begin the disconnection," is
the transmission we just received.

00:36:23.300 --> 00:36:27.590
Transmit to all soldiers. Our primary objective is complete.

00:36:27.800 --> 00:36:30.720
I don't care if this station is obliterated from space.

00:36:30.890 --> 00:36:31.430
Yes, sir!

00:36:45.990 --> 00:36:47.360
Did they think that they had successfully lured me in?

00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:14.230
Verde Buster. First Lieutenant Couza, please return immediately.

00:37:14.240 --> 00:37:16.240
Your energy gage is dangerously low.

00:37:15.220 --> 00:37:18.100
I will never forgive any of you Coordinators!

00:37:27.690 --> 00:37:29.950
First Lieutenant Couza, please return immediately!

00:37:30.070 --> 00:37:32.530
We can see that you've already depleted your energy!

00:37:32.920 --> 00:37:35.760
First Lieutenant Couza, please respond! First Lieutenant Couza!

00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:50.150
Verde Buster. Shams Couza. Signal Lost.

00:37:53.760 --> 00:37:54.800
Our energy is almost completely depleted!

00:37:54.890 --> 00:37:56.720
I know, but we have to at least take this guy down!

00:38:18.010 --> 00:38:21.070
The control room will cease operations,
after this last communications message!

00:38:21.080 --> 00:38:22.670
The 2nd Communications Room will now be–

00:38:24.960 --> 00:38:25.630
Sol.

00:38:25.640 --> 00:38:26.220
What?

00:38:26.640 --> 00:38:28.020
Get off the Gazer.

00:38:29.190 --> 00:38:31.990
Use Apollon A to shoot the enemy ship!

00:38:33.310 --> 00:38:33.980
Sorry.

00:38:39.870 --> 00:38:41.580
Ejection? He threw away his mobile suit?

00:38:46.150 --> 00:38:50.940
Apollon A, use the propulsion laser at 30% and shoot Stargazer.

00:38:51.070 --> 00:38:51.860
I'm going to destroy this guy.

00:38:52.030 --> 00:38:56.530
Selene! If you do that, the sheer force will crush you to pieces!

00:38:57.490 --> 00:38:59.870
Use the rest of the energy and fire at the enemy ship!

00:39:00.200 --> 00:39:01.660
Sol will arrive there soon.

00:39:01.760 --> 00:39:06.640
No. Selene! Didn't you say that we
would build the Stargazer together?!

00:39:08.960 --> 00:39:12.220
We will arrive at the target point in 30 seconds. Don't miss.

00:39:13.270 --> 00:39:14.310
Selene...

00:39:15.090 --> 00:39:17.390
Stargazer, 30 seconds till target!

00:39:19.030 --> 00:39:31.660
25, 24, 23, 22, 21, 20, 19, 18, 17, 16, 15, 14

00:39:25.410 --> 00:39:26.830
I'm all right.

00:39:32.120 --> 00:39:33.250
Selene!

00:39:36.880 --> 00:39:43.630
8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2

00:39:43.630 --> 00:39:44.120
Push it!

00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:48.840
Selene!

00:40:20.490 --> 00:40:22.220
We will now fire at the enemy ship.

00:40:25.850 --> 00:40:28.310
Directly connect the injection router... and the ADF

00:40:28.830 --> 00:40:30.000
Target, set.

00:40:30.460 --> 00:40:32.130
Heat signature approaching from 2 o'clock!

00:40:32.180 --> 00:40:32.550
What?!

00:40:33.760 --> 00:40:34.420
Fire.

00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:47.230
Enemy ship, destroyed.

00:40:47.850 --> 00:40:49.940
Find a communication line to the station.

00:40:50.730 --> 00:40:54.280
Re-activate the life-support systems, starting with the B Ring.

00:41:33.710 --> 00:41:34.550
Are you awake?

00:41:38.650 --> 00:41:40.110
It's best if you don't move.

00:41:40.680 --> 00:41:42.680
Looks as though your rib and collar bones are broken.

00:41:44.060 --> 00:41:46.270
I have no intention of becoming a prisoner of the Coordinators.

00:41:47.200 --> 00:41:49.620
It's not like I will hold you prisoner or anything.

00:41:50.330 --> 00:41:53.590
If you want this back, take it. Although I took out the bullets...

00:41:57.960 --> 00:41:58.970
Where are we?

00:41:59.940 --> 00:42:04.150
I don't know exactly, but we're
somewhere between Earth and Venus.

00:42:07.700 --> 00:42:09.790
I'm taking some energy from your machine.

00:42:10.480 --> 00:42:14.520
This child is having enough trouble just maintaining
the system controls. It's okay with you, right?

00:42:15.080 --> 00:42:16.910
Not as if I have a choice.

00:42:19.000 --> 00:42:21.750
Noir shouldn't have much energy left.

00:42:22.240 --> 00:42:24.320
If we accelerate for 10 seconds, we'll probably use it all up.

00:42:25.170 --> 00:42:27.420
It's barely enough to stop our momentum.

00:42:28.590 --> 00:42:29.880
You're probably right.

00:42:42.840 --> 00:42:44.890
I'm turning the temperature down to 4 degrees.

00:42:44.970 --> 00:42:49.390
Even with the medicine that increases oxygen
absorption, we'll only last about 27 days.

00:42:49.520 --> 00:42:53.810
If we are not discovered by then.
we will become mummies in here.

00:42:55.370 --> 00:42:56.450
Why did you save me?

00:42:58.410 --> 00:42:59.580
I was saddened.

00:43:01.170 --> 00:43:03.370
I was saddened by the thought of dying alone.

00:43:05.030 --> 00:43:09.370
It didn't matter who it was. I just wanted
someone that would talk with me till the end.

00:43:11.510 --> 00:43:16.680
You can squirm if you want. As long as
you make me feel like I'm not alone.

00:43:27.890 --> 00:43:29.390
You're gonna feel a prick.

00:43:35.730 --> 00:43:36.810
You're very quiet.

00:43:38.400 --> 00:43:42.440
Next is me. After the blood flow has
stopped, hold down my arm okay?

00:43:45.660 --> 00:43:50.990
Women have very thin blood vessels. If you don't hold
down properly, they won't come out. Troublesome, right?

00:43:57.760 --> 00:43:58.510
Thanks.

00:44:02.590 --> 00:44:03.880
Now, let's go home.

00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:09.730
Voiture Lumire, open.

00:44:16.570 --> 00:44:21.160
The Stargazer was created for the exploration of outer space.

00:44:21.770 --> 00:44:26.200
It catches the solar wind with its thin curtain of
light particles, and turns it into a propelling force.

00:44:27.110 --> 00:44:34.120
It only moves 0.5 cm in the first second,
but, after a minute, it moves 18 meters.

00:44:34.370 --> 00:44:41.090
After an hour, it's 64 km from where it
started. It achieves a speed of 128 km/h.

00:44:41.970 --> 00:44:45.270
Once it starts moving, it will accelerate forever.

00:44:46.190 --> 00:44:48.520
We can go home. Definitely.

00:44:54.990 --> 00:44:55.900
Are you a bit embarrassed?

00:44:55.900 --> 00:44:56.700
A bit.

00:44:57.990 --> 00:44:59.580
It's only a little further.

00:44:59.780 --> 00:45:02.520
Your senses will become duller and
duller, and you'll become sleepy.

00:45:04.860 --> 00:45:07.610
I have a feeling that I know someone who's just like you.

00:45:09.450 --> 00:45:13.030
Speaking of which, there was once a guy who
said a similar thing when he approached me.

00:45:13.460 --> 00:45:14.840
Even though he's dead.

00:45:14.840 --> 00:45:17.260
Oh, I didn't mean it that way.

00:45:18.470 --> 00:45:19.680
Are you blushing?

00:45:19.680 --> 00:45:20.720
Don't make fun of me.

00:45:22.770 --> 00:45:23.930
What's your name?

00:45:24.000 --> 00:45:24.570
Sven.

00:45:25.270 --> 00:45:26.520
Goodnight, Sven.

00:45:27.060 --> 00:45:28.060
You?

00:45:28.060 --> 00:45:30.860
Me? I'm...

00:47:41.580 --> 00:47:49.150
<i>miageru sora kanashimi no</i>

00:47:41.580 --> 00:47:49.150
As I look to the sky,

00:47:49.320 --> 00:47:57.540
<i>aoki nageki no uta ga tada kikoeru</i>

00:47:49.320 --> 00:47:57.540
I hear only the song of sorrow's blue lament.

00:47:58.110 --> 00:48:05.130
<i>yasashii shiroi matataki</i>

00:47:58.110 --> 00:48:05.130
A gentle white twinkle

00:48:05.590 --> 00:48:13.310
<i>ubaisatta kaze kanata</i>

00:48:05.590 --> 00:48:13.310
was earned off by the wind, into the distance.

00:48:13.590 --> 00:48:21.110
<i>nigenai boku wa kimeta yo</i>

00:48:13.590 --> 00:48:21.110
I decided not to run away.

00:48:21.590 --> 00:48:31.120
<i>kimi no nukumori soba ni kanjite</i>

00:48:21.590 --> 00:48:31.120
I feel your warmth by your side.

00:48:31.580 --> 00:48:39.090
<i>nanika ga kawaru ryoute hirogetara</i>

00:48:31.580 --> 00:48:39.090
If something changes and you open your arms to it,

00:48:39.340 --> 00:48:45.750
<i>sore ga shinjitsu dakara</i>

00:48:39.340 --> 00:48:45.750
that is the truth.

00:48:47.540 --> 00:48:55.210
<i>doko e mo yukazu boku no soba ni ite</i>

00:48:47.550 --> 00:48:55.230
Stay by my side and don't ever leave.

00:48:55.510 --> 00:49:03.470
<i>tobira wo akete ageyou</i>

00:48:55.520 --> 00:49:03.480
I will open the door for you.

00:49:16.580 --> 00:49:24.200
<i>me wo sorasazu ni subete kono mune ni</i>

00:49:16.580 --> 00:49:24.200
Without averting my eyes, I'll keep everything in my heart.

00:49:24.420 --> 00:49:31.260
<i>sasaru shinjitsu naraba</i>

00:49:24.420 --> 00:49:31.260
If it's the sound truth,

00:49:32.510 --> 00:49:40.180
<i>aruite yukou yugami fusagareta</i>

00:49:32.510 --> 00:49:48.530
I'll walk on, beyond the closed door of the stars.

00:49:40.510 --> 00:49:48.520
<i>hoshi no tobira no mukou</i>

00:49:46.900 --> 00:49:53.110
669 Hours Later

00:49:46.900 --> 00:49:53.110
669 Hours Later

00:49:50.030 --> 00:49:52.310
Selene, I've come for you.

00:49:53.900 --> 00:49:56.330
This is the DSSD scout ship, Roclon.

00:49:56.980 --> 00:49:58.650
Selene, please respond.

00:50:00.360 --> 00:50:02.490
Stargazer, please respond.
